00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.760
I am really glad to see that national security&nbsp;
experts are increasingly using a term that I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.720
been talking about on the program for years and&nbsp;
that you may now be familiar with. And that term&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:20.800
is stochastic terrorism to describe what&nbsp;
Donald Trump is doing. We have now heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:28.320
from such national security experts as Juliette&nbsp;
Kayyem and others who are saying that when Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:35.760
Trump goes out there and insists that it's been&nbsp;
stolen and says they must resist and that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:43.040
must fight and that it's an attack on his voters&nbsp;
and democracy and all of these things when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:49.760
makes these claims about electoral fraud that&nbsp;
are both completely unequivocal from Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:58.960
but completely baseless. In fact, Donald Trump is&nbsp;
making it more likely that some of his followers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:04.960
are going to go out and take to the streets&nbsp;
and do real world violence. And the people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:12.000
that sometimes speak on Trump's behalf will&nbsp;
often hide behind. These are sometimes jokes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.600
that are being told or things are being taken&nbsp;
too literally or whatever the case may be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.800
But as Juliette Kayyem points out, and this is&nbsp;
written about in a very good Mother Jones article,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:29.440
we've also heard from others like Kori Schake and&nbsp;
other people. This can really encourage people to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:34.800
go completely crazy with real world violence. And&nbsp;
the term stochastic terrorism refers to the idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:44.240
that stochastic terror terrorism refers&nbsp;
to random but predictable violence. OK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:50.800
if my audience is big enough and I every day&nbsp;
say somebody should really do something about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:57.840
Joe Joe Schmoe, something somebody really needs to&nbsp;
deal with. The problem of Joe Schmoe, Joe Schmoe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.080
is attacking our way of life. Joe Schmoe, if he's&nbsp;
allowed to continue doing what he's doing, is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.840
going to be the end of America as we know it. If&nbsp;
my audience is big enough, it becomes predictable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:13.760
that someone in my audience is going to take that&nbsp;
to heart and commit an act of real world violence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.560
Now, it will be random in terms of who does it,&nbsp;
where and when. That's that's where the term&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.360
stochastic terrorism comes from. We're talking&nbsp;
about a confidence interval. We're talking about,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:29.440
you know, it refers to terms often used in&nbsp;
finance and science and relating to distributions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:35.040
But if the if you're speaking to enough people,&nbsp;
it becomes predictable that somebody is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.680
to take action. And that is exactly what a lot&nbsp;
of national security experts are now saying.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:46.480
And senior federal law enforcement officials have&nbsp;
been saying that the level of concern is extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:52.320
high, that they are seeing threatening rhetoric&nbsp;
and levels of anger as a result of the things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:57.120
that Donald Trump and his defenders who continue&nbsp;
to claim he actually won. Joe Biden didn't really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:03.200
win. It was stolen. There was fraud. It's all part&nbsp;
of the conspiracy. This is something that is very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.760
dangerous. And I'm glad to see national security&nbsp;
